      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-369",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-369 - Unknown vulnerability type\nVulnerability: Division by Zero in RPN Calculator Stack Operations\nDescription: A division by zero vulnerability exists in the main_loop() function of the RPN calculator.\nWhen processing division (/) or modulo (%) operations, the code does not validate that\nthe divisor (r2) is non-zero before performing the arithmetic operation. This occurs in\nthe switch case handlers at lines 188 and 194 in stackmachine.c, where the two_arg_operand\nmacro executes r1 / r2 or r1 % r2 without checking if r2 equals zero.\n\nAn attacker can craft input that pushes a value onto the stack followed by zero, then\ntriggers a division or modulo operation. This causes a Floating Point Exception (FPE)\nsignal (SIGFPE), resulting in program termination and denial of service.\n\nThe vulnerability can be exploited with input such as \"10 0 /\" which pushes 10 and 0\nonto the stack, then attempts division, causing an immediate crash. The patch adds\nvalidation checks (if (r2 != 0)) before executing these operations to prevent the FPE.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "cp-tkctf-rpn-calculator-source/stackmachine.c"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 188,
                  "endLine": 188,
                  "startColumn": 17,
                  "endColumn": 17
                }
              },
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "name": "main_loop",
                  "kind": "function"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
